    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The story of urbanisation in Kenya is one of cautious optimism with 27 per cent of the population living in urban areas, a figure that is  increasing by an estimated 4.3 per cent a year . In Nairobi, the emphasis on developing \n       gray infrastructure  has resulted in inadequate green spaces, and consequently, raised concerns for the amount of natural spaces children can access.",
